---
import Default from '@astrojs/starlight/components/Hero.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const steps = [
	{ what: 'Install it on the server that runs Postgres', cmd: `curl -fsSL https://pgbx.deemwar.com/install.sh | sh` },
	{ what: 'Tell it your storage bucket (it asks you)', cmd: 'sudo pgbx setup server' },
	{ what: 'Restart Postgres once (setup prints the exact command)', cmd: 'sudo systemctl restart postgresql' },
];
const trust = [
	"Uses Postgres's own pg_dump",
	'Restores into a new database, never over yours',
	'Nothing changes until you run setup',
	'Backups go to your bucket, not to us',
	'Tested on Postgres 13–18',
	'MIT licensed',
];
const asks = [
	{ you: 'Is my database backed up?', cmd: 'pgbx status --json' },
	{ you: "Why did last night's backup fail?", cmd: 'pgbx doctor --json' },
	{ you: "Restore yesterday's copy of shop so I can check it", cmd: 'pgbx db-restore --db shop --into shop_check --time 2026-10-01T23:00:00Z' },
	{ you: 'How many orders came in today?', note: 'reuses the query you saved in ~/pgbx/prod/shop/memories.md', cmd: `pgbx query "SELECT count(*) FROM orders WHERE created_at > now() - interval '1 day'"` },
];
---

<div class="product-hero">
	<Default />
	<section class="steps" aria-label="Set up in three steps">
		<ol>
			{steps.map((s, i) => (
				<li>
					<span class="n">{i + 1}</span>
					<div class="body">
						<p class="what">{s.what}</p>
						<div class="cmd">
							<code>{s.cmd}</code>
							<button type="button" class="copy" data-cmd={s.cmd} aria-label={`Copy: ${s.cmd}`}>Copy</button>
						</div>
					</div>
				</li>
			))}
		</ol>
		<p class="done">
			That's it. Every database on that server is now backed up every night, and new ones within a minute.
			Check any time with <code>pgbx status</code>. Need it back? <a href={`${base}/guides/disaster-recovery/`}>One command restores it</a>, even onto a new server.
		</p>
		<ul class="trust">
			{trust.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
		</ul>
		<div class="agent" id="agents">
			<h2>Or let your AI agent look after it</h2>
			<p>
				pgbx comes with a skill for Claude Code and Codex. Ask in plain words; the agent runs the matching
				<code>pgbx</code> command on your server, over SSH, without a shell. Every command has a
				<a href={`${base}/concepts/safety-tiers/`}>safety level</a>: anything that pauses backups or deletes old ones
				is refused unless you say yes, and no command ever overwrites a live database.
			</p>
			<ul class="asks">
				{asks.map((a) => (
					<li>
						<span class="you">“{a.you}”</span>
						<code>{a.cmd}</code>
						{a.note && <span class="note">{a.note}</span>}
					</li>
				))}
			</ul>
			<p class="skill">Each database gets its own memory, <code>~/pgbx/&lt;connection&gt;/&lt;db&gt;/memories.md</code> and
				<code>tables.md</code>: the agent reads it first and writes to it only when you say "remember this".
				<a href={`${base}/agents/skill/#memory-one-folder-per-database`}>How memory works</a>.</p>
			<p class="skill">Add it with <code>pgbx skill install</code> (the installer offers it too).</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</div>

<script>
	for (const b of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.steps .copy')) {
		b.addEventListener('click', async () => {
			try {
				await navigator.clipboard.writeText(b.dataset.cmd ?? '');
				b.textContent = 'Copied';
			} catch {
				b.textContent = 'Select it';
			}
			setTimeout(() => (b.textContent = 'Copy'), 1500);
		});
	}
</script>

<style>
	.product-hero {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
	}
	.steps {
		width: min(100% - 2rem, 46rem);
		margin: 0 auto 1rem;
	}
	.steps ol {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}
	.steps li {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.875rem;
		align-items: flex-start;
		margin: 0;
	}
	.n {
		flex: none;
		width: 1.75rem;
		height: 1.75rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		display: grid;
		place-items: center;
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		background: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
		color: var(--sl-color-accent-high);
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-accent);
		margin-top: 0.1rem;
	}
	.body {
		flex: 1;
		min-width: 0;
	}
	.what {
		margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}
	.cmd {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		padding: 0.5rem 0.5rem 0.5rem 0.875rem;
	}
	.cmd code {
		flex: 1;
		min-width: 0;
		overflow-x: auto;
		white-space: nowrap;
		background: none;
		padding: 0;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
	}
	.copy {
		flex: none;
		font: inherit;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		cursor: pointer;
		border-radius: 0.375rem;
		padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-4);
		background: transparent;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}
	.copy:hover {
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
		border-color: var(--sl-color-accent);
	}
	.done {
		margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}
	.trust {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 1rem 0 0;
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
	}
	.agent {
		margin-top: 2.25rem;
		padding-top: 1.5rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
	}
	.agent h2 {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-h4);
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
	}
	.agent p {
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		margin: 0;
	}
	.asks {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 1rem 0 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.6rem;
	}
	.asks li {
		margin: 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.25rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		padding: 0.6rem 0.875rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
	}
	.you {
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}
	.asks code {
		background: none;
		padding: 0;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		color: var(--sl-color-accent-high);
		overflow-x: auto;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}
	.asks .note {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}
	.agent .skill {
		margin-top: 0.875rem;
	}
	.trust li {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
		border-radius: 999px;
		padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem;
	}
</style>
